management code are original to Arange-tun by Amin Mohammadi.

The built-in "Rathole v2" tunnel (internal/rathole) is a Go reimplementation of
the rathole reverse-proxy protocol by rapiz1 and contributors
(https://github.com/rapiz1/rathole), which is licensed under the Apache License
2.0. No rathole source code is copied; the protocol — its control/data-channel
handshake, message framing, and forwarding design — was reimplemented in Go from
the published specification and source.

The "IP Spoofing" transport (the spoof_* config keys; the spoof carrier in
internal/utils/network/spoof*.go and the KCP integration in kcp.go; the
per-side spoofpipe transports; the spoof tester in internal/spooftest and
internal/manage/spooftest.go) is derived from Backpack by Amin Mohammadi
(AminMGMT) — https://github.com/AminMGMT/backpack — which is licensed under the
GNU Affero General Public License v3.0, the same licence as this project. The
code was ported with attribution under that licence; the tunnel token salts and
module paths were adapted to Arange-tun.

The multi-exit health failover and scoring (health_failover; the steering in
internal/utils/network/endpoints.go and internal/utils/network/healthscore.go;
internal/manage/exithealth.go) and the game-latency tester (internal/manage/
game.go and gamemenu.go, and RecommendFEC in internal/manage/benchmark.go) are
also derived from Backpack by Amin Mohammadi (AminMGMT), under the same AGPL-3.0
licence and with attribution.

The sniffer/monitor bind-address handling (web_bind; internal/web/monitorhttp.go
and the monitorBind default) is likewise derived from Backpack by Amin Mohammadi
(AminMGMT), under the same AGPL-3.0 licence and with attribution.

The "Throughput" performance preset (PresetThroughput in internal/manage/
preset.go, and its KCP-family gating in setup/edit/create) is derived from
Backpack by Amin Mohammadi (AminMGMT), under the same AGPL-3.0 licence and with
attribution; the preset's tuning numbers were re-fitted to this fork's own
Balance/Turbo/Aggressive baselines.
